            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Conversion Optimization Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>

                ```
                <p>
                    Conversion performance can be affected by many factors across a digital
                    product. Identifying the actual cause of conversion problems is important
                    before making changes to customer-facing experiences.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Complex User Journeys:</b> Customers may abandon a process when it
                    contains too many steps or requires unnecessary information. Simplifying
                    workflows can make important actions easier to complete.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Unclear Value Proposition:</b> Customers may not understand why they
                    should use a product or complete an action. Clear messaging can communicate
                    the product's value and expected benefits more effectively.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Weak Calls to Action:</b> Important actions should be clearly visible
                    and understandable. Effective calls to action can help customers understand
                    what they should do next.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Lack of Trust:</b> Customers may hesitate when they do not have enough
                    confidence in a product, service, or transaction. Clear information,
                    transparent processes, and relevant trust signals can reduce uncertainty.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Poor Mobile Experience:</b> A product that works well on desktop but
                    provides a difficult mobile experience can create unnecessary conversion
                    barriers. Responsive and mobile-friendly journeys are important for
                    customers using different devices.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <b>Insufficient Data:</b> Optimization decisions can become unreliable
                    when teams do not have enough information about customer behavior.
                    Establishing appropriate measurement and analytics helps create a stronger
                    basis for improvement.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="col-lg-4 text-center">
                @* Add the relevant conversion challenges image here when available. *@
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    ```

